        "original_id": "894fbe09-2111-5f0b-bb11-1ec2ba4d7049",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jimmy Hoffa, Jack Nicholson, Danny DeVito, David Mamet, John Joseph Nicholson, Robert Ciaro, László Kovács, Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, Sally Struthers\n- Films: Hoffa, Five Easy Pieces, Easy Rider\n- Organizations: Teamsters\n- Roles: actor, filmmaker, director, writer, cinematographer, Teamsters leader\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Nicholson was born as John Joseph Nicholson on April 22, 1937, and he is an American actor and filmmaker who has performed for over 60 years.\n- László Kovács became most famous for his award-winning cinematography on the films Easy Rider (1969) and Five Easy Pieces (1970).\n- Five Easy Pieces stars Jack Nicholson, and its supporting cast includes Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, and Sally Struthers.\n- László Kovács received numerous awards during his career, including three Lifetime Achievement Awards.\n- Hoffa is a 1992 French-American biographical crime film directed by Danny DeVito and written by David Mamet.\n- Hoffa is based on the life of Jimmy Hoffa, who was a Teamsters leader.\n- In Hoffa, Jack Nicholson plays Jimmy Hoffa, and Danny DeVito plays Robert Ciaro, a composite character based on several Hoffa associates over the years.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
